      "message": "In this CL, the speed feature `switchable_lr_with_bias_level` is added to restrict loop restoration search to RESTORE_SWITCHABLE by skipping RD cost comparison of RESTORE_WIENER and RESTORE_SGRPROJ. It also applies a 0.5% selection penalty per level to Wiener and SGR filter types in `search_switchable()` biasing towards no LR filtering.\n\nSince frame-level selection of RESTORE_WIENER or RESTORE_SGRPROJ can still include a mix of filtered and NONE blocks, applying bias during individual Wiener/SGR searches (`search_wiener(), search_sgrproj()`) may not yield the intended effect. To address this, frame-level selection of WIENER and SGRPROJ is disabled, and the bias is applied during `search_switchable()`, where all three types (NONE, WIENER, SGRPROJ) RD cost is compared ensuring intended effect.\n\nPerformance results of encoder and decoder for the streams generated\nwith low complexity decode enabled.\n```\n                        Instruction Count                                                                 \n                           Reduction(%)                        BD-Rate Loss(%)                Time Reduction(%)\ncpu-used  Resolution    Encoder   Decoder    avg.psnr  ovr.psnr    ssim      vmaf    vmaf_neg   dav1d Decoder   \n   1          608P      -0.278     1.453      0.0883    0.0777    0.1412    0.0081   -0.0358       1.339\n   1        HDRES2      -0.166     1.763      0.1293    0.1362    0.1387    0.2373    0.2445       1.414\n   1       Average      -0.227     1.594      0.1069    0.1043    0.1401    0.1123    0.0916       1.373\n                                                                                                   \n   2          608P      -0.157     0.908      0.1020    0.1013    0.1147    0.1461    0.0666       1.023\n   2        HDRES2      -0.132     1.314      0.1104    0.1091    0.1335    0.4946    0.3270       1.175\n   2       Average      -0.146     1.092      0.1058    0.1049    0.1232    0.3045    0.1850    